{"uid":"22c82a9d0dba75fa","name":"test_cold_no_index_legacy_shapes_render_the_exact_full_tail_on_both_hub_surfaces[interleaved-no-earlier-text-delta]","fullName":"tests.test_log_merge_bounded_reads#test_cold_no_index_legacy_shapes_render_the_exact_full_tail_on_both_hub_surfaces","historyId":"ef69df58b5591e8af332ac3348a5b53f","time":{"start":1791946220484,"stop":1791946227028,"duration":6544},"description":"Task 014 (PRD C.3): the cold, NO-index read on the transcript\n    shapes the indexed performance scenarios above measure\n    (`_write_iteration_with_older_thinking_marker`, and\n    `_write_iteration_with_interleaved_ignored_suffix` at both\n    alignments, 100,000 older `ignored` events each) -- with neither\n    `render_index.json` nor `collapse_index.json` present, before or\n    after -- renders exactly the full renderer's last 200 lines through\n    `ui_server.rendered_log_lines` on both surfaces: the dead-run on-disk\n    fallback and the live branch proxied through the real engine\n    `GET /logs` ASGI handler.\n\n    This is a correctness control only, with no byte cap: without an\n    index the hub cannot know a disclosed-unresolved collapse flag's\n    right value without scanning back for it, and pays that scan. The\n    `earlier-hidden-text-delta` variant is why no cheaper guess is\n    allowed: one `text_delta` halfway through the older history (far\n    outside any bounded read) sets `textSeen`, so every visible\n    `message_end` text below it is an already-streamed replay the full\n    renderer suppresses -- the same transcript without it must print\n    that text. A guessed flag gets exactly one of the two variants\n    wrong.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 014 (PRD C.3): the cold, NO-index read on the transcript<br />\nshapes the indexed performance scenarios above measure<br />\n(<code>_write_iteration_with_older_thinking_marker</code>, and<br />\n<code>_write_iteration_with_interleaved_ignored_suffix</code> at both<br />\nalignments, 100,000 older <code>ignored</code> events each) -- with neither<br />\n<code>render_index.json</code> nor <code>collapse_index.json</code> present, before or<br />\nafter -- renders exactly the full renderer's last 200 lines through<br />\n<code>ui_server.rendered_log_lines</code> on both surfaces: the dead-run on-disk<br />\nfallback and the live branch proxied through the real engine<br />\n<code>GET /logs</code> ASGI handler.</p>\n<pre><code>This is a correctness control only, with no byte cap: without an\nindex the hub cannot know a disclosed-unresolved collapse flag's\nright value without scanning back for it, and pays that scan. The\n`earlier-hidden-text-delta` variant is why no cheaper guess is\nallowed: one `text_delta` halfway through the older history (far\noutside any bounded read) sets `textSeen`, so every visible\n`message_end` text below it is an already-streamed replay the full\nrenderer suppresses -- the same transcript without it must print\nthat text. A guessed flag gets exactly one of the two variants\nwrong.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791946220436,"stop":1791946220437,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791946220437,"stop":1791946220449,"duration":12},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791946220449,"stop":1791946220450,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentS